---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1><span class="hl-title">About</span></h1>

    <p class="placeholder-note meta">
      (Placeholder — rewrite this in first person, specific and true. The notes
      below are prompts, not copy to ship.)
    </p>

    <p>
      Start with something concrete and a little unexpected — not a job title.
      Where you’re from, what you were doing at 2pm on a random Tuesday, the
      thing you’d talk about for an hour without being asked twice.
    </p>

    <p>
      A paragraph on how you actually spend time. The spec suggests
      motorcycling and books — if that’s true, say what kind, name the last one
      that mattered, admit the one everyone loves that you couldn’t finish.
      Specifics do the work here; vague enthusiasm reads as filler.
    </p>

    <h2>What I care about in the work</h2>
    <p>
      One honest belief about how you like to build — ideally one you arrived
      at by being wrong first. Not “I value quality.” Something with a scar on
      it.
    </p>

    <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
    <p>
      Links out — GitHub, email, anywhere worth pointing to. Keep it to the
      handful that actually matter.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .placeholder-note {
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
  .prose :global(h2) {
    color: var(--accent-heading);
  }
</style>
